# R2 time-split MSE decomposition (PR #6 finding R2 + correction 2)
# date: 2026-10-13 13:50:51  python: Python 3.12.14
#
# Question: replace the P2-era mechanism labels in README with the exact
# decomposition of GIN-ens-minus-RF R2 on the committed time splits.
#
# Method: SSE/n = (ybar-pbar)^2 + sigma_y^2 * f(s,r), f = s^2+1-2rs,
#   s = sigma_pred/sigma_y, r = corr(pred, y). Level has no interaction
#   with (s,r); the spread/correlation pair shares the r*s cross-term, so
#   their allocation is the 2-player Shapley split (level direct).
#   Contribution to dR2 = -(d SSE/n)/sigma_y^2; residual = dR2 - sum.
#
# Inputs (committed): results/rf_preds_{tag}_time.npz +
#   results/gnn_preds_{tag}_time{,_seed1,_seed2}.npz; constant_r2 from
#   results/time_split/summary.csv.
#
# Note on the one 3rd-decimal difference vs the PR #6 reference table:
#   egfr correlation is -0.044479 at full precision -> -0.044 at 3dp;
#   the review's -0.045 appears to be a double-rounding of -0.04448.
#   Current committed data wins; README writes -0.044.
#
# Command:
#   .venv/bin/python /tmp/r2_time_decomp.py
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
